# TEST_ID=GBP-VIDEO-003
# BUILD_ID=color-0001
# DOL=gbp-video-color-probe
# COMMIT=9d8302d
# COMMIT_FULL=9d8302d6cf05b7f4eb913080cb024bb4951954c6
# DOL_SHA256=cc88e4c45559f11047ca657b78045e2fd2c5d646a1b68e7e453fcf796d177cf4
# LOG_SHA256=28c5a06c8c852802b014fe8c97780d8e3a751166ad41be2e979e71ecb3f3bb8c
# LOG_SIZE=40790
# BLOCKS=hw-gamecube-gbp-2026-09-18-color-0001-color.bin
# BLOCKS_SHA256=95595f9d9eb4945e42ee1653ade5a1cd72a3646d698cad254d32c84ba0762bb7
# BLOCKS_SIZE=461684
# BLOCKS_FORMAT=OGBPCOL1 v1
# CAPTURED=2026-09-18
# NOTE=FIRST PHYSICAL RUN OF GBP-VIDEO-003, EXECUTED 2026-09-18, one run, with a Game Pak present (CONTROL orig=92, bit 0x02 set) carrying the controlled eight-bar AGB colour stimulus. The runtime reached its own target: stop=color_certified (8), three eligible frames certified with identical sig[40], capture 0.072 s inside a 30 s safety budget of which 5.179 s were used. This run does NOT close U-GBP-011; see the gate note below.
# NOTE=THE FIXED PRE-HANDLER WAIT WAS SUFFICIENT IN ITS INTENDED POSITION. PREHANDLERWAIT ms=5000 want_ticks=202500000 elapsed=202500008 (5.00000020 s at 40.5 MHz), 78307393 iterations, done=1 (the time bound, not the iteration cap); CONTROL 8e -> 8e, IRQ 0500 -> 0500, INTSR 00012000 -> 00012000 across the wait. After it, capture opened and the first eligible frame appeared at frame index 2 of 5, with the certified run starting immediately. The claim is sufficiency of 5000 ms at that position on this unit under these conditions, and nothing more. GBP-HW-120.
# NOTE=SERVICE AND RESTORE WERE CLEAN. 440 deliveries = acks = rearms = unmasks (162 VIDEO, 288 AUDIO); 0 timeouts, 0 busy, 0 uncertain, 0 overflow, 0 errors; R3 reported 0 semantic disagreements in this run. Teardown restored CONTROL, IRQ, PI, AR_INFO and the handler with readback, intmr_final=000001fa. OGBPCOL1 v1 sidecar validated offline: header CRC 96002fc9 and total CRC 19ebfbda both recomputed and matching, footer OGBPCEND at 0x70B68, size == off_footer+12. GBP-HW-121.
# NOTE=THE OFFICIAL ANALYSER STOPPED AT ITS OWN GATE AND THAT VERDICT STANDS. tools/vcolor.py, run unmodified, reports VERDICT: INCONCLUSIVE - CERTIFIED RAW MISMATCH: the three certified frames are NOT byte-identical over the full 153 600-byte raw frame. First difference at byte 0x108 - block 0, x=66, y=0, byte 0 of the group - 83 vs 03. Pairwise differing bytes: A/B 2125, B/C 2073, A/C 2137, touching all 40 blocks and all 160 rows. GBP-HW-122.
# NOTE=EVERY DIFFERENCE IS IN A BYTE NEITHER REFERENCE DECODER READS. Per byte-in-group, A/B 0:1878 1:0 2:247 3:0; B/C 0:1815 1:0 2:258 3:0; A/C 0:1860 1:0 2:277 3:0. Bytes 1 and 3 - the only bytes the Start-up Disc and GBI consume (GBP-VID-003, recorded 2026-09-16, two days before this run) - differ in ZERO positions across all three pairs. Under the pre-existing projection word = (b1 << 8) | b3 the three certified frames are identical in 38 400 of 38 400 words. GBP-HW-123.
# NOTE=POST-GATE DIAGNOSTIC PROJECTION. Because the official gate did not pass, what follows is a diagnostic projection and NOT a closure of U-GBP-011. Per 30-pixel bar, every bar uniform (one distinct colour15 each) and identical in A, B and C: stimulus 0x0000 0x001F 0x03E0 0x7C00 0x7FFF 0x0001 0x0020 0x0400 was observed as 0x0000 0x7C00 0x03E0 0x001F 0x7FFF 0x0400 0x0020 0x0001. H1 (outer-group swap, the references' RGB5A3 reading with R = bits 14-10) matches 8/8 bars exactly. H2 (verbatim AGB BGR555) matches 4/8, and those four are exactly the swap-invariant colours that carry no discriminating information. The post-gate diagnostic projection matches H1 exactly. U-GBP-011 remains OPEN. GBP-HW-124.
# NOTE=FLAG15 ISOLATED FROM THE COLOUR PAYLOAD FOR THE FIRST TIME. Exactly one word per certified frame has bit 15 set, at x=0 y=0, and here the word is exactly 0x8000: flag set, colour15 = 0x0000, because the stimulus paints bar 0 black and writes bit 15 as zero everywhere. Every earlier physical frame had that word as 0xFFFF (flag over white 0x7FFF), where bit 15 cannot be distinguished from the colour. Count and position reproduce the earlier fixtures exactly - one per frame at word 0 in vstate-0001/0003/0004, and 3 of 88 stored blocks in GBP-VIDEO-001, all at word 0. GBP-HW-125.
# NOTE=THE BYTES 0/2 BEHAVIOUR IS PRE-EXISTING, NOT NEW. GBP-VID-003 (2026-09-16) records that bytes 0 and 2 are read by neither reference decoder. GBP-HW-058 records the physical byte-doubling break in 5 of 960 groups. GBP-HW-070 measures 688 byte-0 exceptions in 84 480 words of GBP-VIDEO-001 and states that byte 0 variability does not alter what either reference reads, with the cause open in U-GBP-029; U-GBP-021 already forbids consuming byte 0. src/gbp/gbp_vsig.h excludes bytes 0 and 2 from the runtime signature for exactly that reason. Re-measured this round on sig-identical frame pairs of the earlier fixtures: class0/class1/class2/class3 = 584/0/46/0 (vstate-0001), 97/0/25/0 (vstate-0003), 292/0/19/0 (vstate-0004) - the same shape as this run.
# NOTE=ONE GENUINELY NEW OBSERVATION ABOUT BYTE 2. GBP-HW-070 recorded byte 2 never differing from byte 3 (0 cases) in GBP-VIDEO-001, and this round reproduces that 688/0 result exactly from the stored fixture. Byte 2 DOES vary in the later fixtures (8712, 8679 and 8907 words of 576 000 in vstate-0001/0003/0004) and in this run. That variability was latent in fixtures already committed but had never been measured or registered; it is recorded here as a NEW OBSERVATION derived from pre-existing fixtures plus color-0001, and it is not evidence that anything changed in the device.
# NOTE=THE GATE'S DOCUMENTED PURPOSE. HARDWARE_TESTS.md V3.25 and tools/vcolor.py state it in one sentence - "a checksum can collide; the bytes cannot" - so the full-raw comparison exists to protect the runtime's cheap sig[40] stability decision from a collision, and NOT as a claim that bytes 0 and 2 are part of the picture. The gate is therefore stricter than the question it guards. It is not weakened, edited or reinterpreted here; OGBPCOL1 v1 and tools/vcolor.py stay exactly as frozen, and this run stays INCONCLUSIVE under them.
# NOTE=IDENTITY WARNING. What was physically executed is build color-0001 at commit 9d8302d, the DOL in build/poc/gbp-video-color-probe at that commit, sha256 cc88e4c4... The device log records the commit and build id, not a DOL hash, so that hash is the build tree's at the declared commit. A rebuild at any other commit produces a DIFFERENT hash, because the commit identity is embedded in the image, and inherits the source behaviour but NOT the physical status. Compare hashes before calling any rebuilt DOL the tested artifact. build/swiss/11-color/boot.dol is a byte copy of the build tree DOL, not a separate identity.
# NOTE=THIS SCRIPT IS A PREFIX, NOT THE RUN, exactly as in the vstate fixtures: it carries the 003A stage, the pre-handler wait, the verify cycles and the teardown - the only parts whose transport operations the log records. The 440 service cycles were never written line by line and are NOT invented here. The sidecar is the evidence for them: 5 frame records, 3 certified, 3 raw frames of 153 600 bytes at offsets 0, 153600 and 307200, ring slots 2, 3 and 0, all three with sig0 7780f781 and sig39 f780f780.
# NOTE=THE SOURCE LOG DECLARES truncated=1. The truncated line is PREHANDLERWAIT, which hit the logger's 255-character limit and ends at "intmr_po", exactly the same instrumentation defect already registered for the vstate-prewait-5000 run. It costs nothing here either: ms, want_ticks, begin, end, elapsed, iters, done and both CONTROL/IRQ/INTSR snapshots are complete before the cut, and only the trailing intmr_post value is lost while INTMR is reported in full elsewhere in the log. Registered as an INSTRUMENTATION DEFECT / NON-BLOCKING.
